### Evolution

The good thing is, if you start thinking about this, you can intuitively answer these questions yourself.

It might not be the easiest, because it requires you to think, but if you understand, you will understand how to create relationships. 

The short answer:

Ask yourself, from an evolutionary point of view: What's attractive?

Is it desperation? Stress? Weakness? Having no opinion? Having no goal besides finding a relationship? 

Or is it competence, strength, self-reliance, being decisive, knowing what you want, having ambitions? Being generous? emotional stability? stability? humor?

Why are those things attractive? Because of how men and women are built biologically.

The long answer:

Men are biologically built to quickly share their seed, while women are biologically built to having to carry a child for 9 months. 

And as much as we wish to separate ourselves from our "stupid silly" biology, it has a psychological effect, even if you don't wish to bring up a child.

Women are built to filter through men and test them by their strength, stability and so on in order to weigh if they are a good choice for something they potentially have to carry 9 months around and then for 18 years at least. So they test men.

Men are built to provide and protect. To being relied on and to provide strength.

And even when those traditional images of gender roles are fading away, they still dominate our biology and psychology.

And you could say: That's unfair! I don't want to be tested, measured up and compared. And I understand that!

But that's not necessarily bad. Because if you are able to differentiate yourself, you are able to integrate yourself with somebody else - like a puzzle piece. By having an edge - you two actually fit together. You won't and you shouldn't just settle for "any" relationship. You should find the right one! If you're round and try to not have any style by fitting in everywhere, you will fit in nowhere. That's the power of polarity.

So first become who you are - by developing your potential. Finding your own style, finding what you want to do with your life, finding your wisdom and strength. Then you're able to find where you belong.

Why are woman and man built like this? Because evolution wants you to grow. It grows by testing your strength. Women take that task by testing you. And you are able to grow. 

You don't have to become perfect. You don't need to become the "666" of male power (6-pack, 6-figure-salary, 6-foot tall). It's a proxy for the stakes of attractiveness (strength, capability, biological fitness).

What your body is lacking, you can even out with wisdom and emotional strength - if that's your strength.

What your emotional intelligence is lacking, you can even out with working out - if that's your strength.

Strengthen your strengths, but don't entirely neglect everything else.


### Optimierung


That sounds exactly like me, some years ago! I still fall into that trap sometimes. All my life has been about freeing myself from negative emotions, negative environments and negative stuff. Finding purpose, making a business.. I know it all too well.

Earlier this year, I tried to hustle to my business doing 5 months of social media, building software products, etc. But the essential wisdom I took away from these months is one thing: Nothing good comes from (dis)stress.

Nothing good comes from making a fuss, always searching, always doing, never resting. Always being serious about everything.

One of our most important abilities as humans is to play. It allows us to dance, to flirt, to experiment, to be curious.

And once I started to become more relaxed and playful, I landed a high ticket client within 15 minutes. Lesson learned.

I believe there is a healthy side to what you do. I love philosophy! Learning about all these things, and what's beneath them. But try to find your own way too. Your own voice, your own opinion - even if we are "just" a mirror of our environment. Decide what's good for you and what's garbage (garbage in - garbage out).

But the biggest garbage in your system, in all of your life, is to think you have to become somebody else.

By all means: grow, become more capable, become strong and evolve. But do it being playful and curious.

Those who seek knowledge,
Collect something every day.
Those who seek meaning,
Let go of something every day.

Tao Te King - verse 48


